── UNKNOWN NAME ────────────────────────────── E0211_python_int.lt:2:11  [E0211]

Stilt has no `int` function: a value converts with a method, as `x.to_i64()`:

  2 │   let n = int("42")
    │           ^^^

A number converts with a method, as `n.to_i64()` or `n.to_f64()`, and a string
parses with the same methods, which give an `Option`, `None` when the text isn't
a number.
